    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** stands out as our premier start with an elite 81.26 score. While his base projection is solid, the optimizer is heavily bullish on his matchup against Hunter Dobbins, with a dynamic platoon advantage boosting his output by 14% and a leadoff slot assignment providing a critical 10% lift. **Yordan Alvarez** (65.52) and **Junior Caminero** (62.27) anchor the heart of the lineup despite facing tough arms like Bryan Woo and Trevor Rogers, respectively; **Yordan Alvarez** maintains an elite 0.465 xwOBA that makes him nearly impossible to sit regardless of the matchup, while **Junior Caminero** leverages a strong order position (#3) to maintain his high floor. **Kyle Schwarber** also warrants attention; his 60.39 score is bolstered by his role as the table-setter, where his leadoff spot provides a 10% efficiency premium against Kremer.\n\nConversely, we are exercising caution with **Christian Yelich** and **Gary Sanchez**, both of whom are facing the high-caliber Tarik Skubal. **Christian Yelich** drops to a 39.01 score, falling just below our operational floor, as the combination of an elite arm and a negative platoon split stifles his upside. **Gary Sanchez** barely clears the threshold at 42.06, largely because he is neutral-to-favorable in platoon, but he is clearly tethered to the assumption that he hits #5 in the order. Our most difficult bench decision involved **Pedro Ramirez**, whose 47.45 score made him the strongest candidate for a spot start. Ultimately, the optimizer prioritized the higher-ceiling utility of **Junior Caminero** and the specific platoon-gains found in the outfield slots, leaving **Pedro Ramirez** on the bench due to his projected #7 slot, which carries a detrimental 3% penalty in our model. We are monitoring the status of **Gary Sanchez**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Yordan Alvarez** closely; as their lineups are currently pending, any shift in their batting order could necessitate a last-minute adjustment to maximize our stolen base and runs potential.",
